.TH CALPOP 1 "2026-11-24" "calpop 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
calpop \- a calendar popup for Wayland bars
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B calpop
.RB [ \-c
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B calpop
.B \-\-default\-config
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B calpop
opens a small month calendar anchored under (or above) your bar.
Running it again closes it, so it can be used directly as the click
command of a bar module, for example Waybar's
.B on\-click
on the clock, or bound to a key.
.PP
It needs a Wayland compositor that supports the wlr\-layer\-shell
protocol (Hyprland, KDE Plasma, Sway, river, niri, Wayfire, labwc\&...).
GNOME and X11 are not supported.
.PP
There is no agenda: no events, no reminders, no network access.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Read the configuration from
.I PATH
instead of the default location.
.TP
.B \-\-default\-config
Print a configuration file that lists every setting with its default
value and a short explanation, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH CLOSING
The popup closes with
.BR Esc " or " q ,
with a click anywhere outside it on the same screen, or when
.B calpop
is run again.
While it is open it takes the keyboard, like a menu.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR "Left" ", " "h" ", " "Page Up"
Previous month.
.TP
.BR "Right" ", " "l" ", " "Page Down"
Next month.
.TP
.BR "Up" ", " "k"
Previous year.
.TP
.BR "Down" ", " "j"
Next year.
.TP
.BR "Home" ", " "t"
Back to the current month.
.PP
The mouse wheel moves one month per notch.
Clicking the title or the date at the bottom goes back to today.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration is read from
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/calpop/config.toml ,
by default
.IR ~/.config/calpop/config.toml ,
each time the popup opens: no restart is needed.
Every key is optional.
To start from a file that lists them all:
.PP
.RS
.B calpop \-\-default\-config > ~/.config/calpop/config.toml
.RE
.PP
Main settings: first day of the week, week numbers (ISO 8601, US or
from the locale), language of day and month names, position (screen
edge, alignment, margins, screen), font, colors, corner radius,
opacity.
.PP
Colors can come from a theme file, so the popup follows a theme that
changes with the wallpaper.
.B theme
points to a file with lines in one of these forms, and colors are then
written
.BR @name :
.PP
.RS
.nf
@define\-color name #rrggbb;   (GTK, Waybar, matugen, wallust)
\-\-name: #rrggbb;              (CSS variables, pywal)
name = "#rrggbb"              (Omarchy)
.fi
.RE
.SH STYLE
A
.I style.css
file next to
.I config.toml
is applied last and can change anything with GTK4 CSS.
Classes:
.BR calpop\-root " (the popup), " title ", " nav " (arrows), "
.BR weekday ", " week " (week numbers), " day
.RB "(with " today ", " weekend ", " other ),
.BR footer .
For example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&.day { font\-weight: bold; }
\&.today { border\-radius: 6px; }
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LC_TIME
Language of day and month names and, with
.BR first_day " or " week_numbering " set to " locale ,
the week rules.
The
.B locale
setting overrides it, and
.BR LC_ALL ,
for calpop only.
.TP
.B GSK_RENDERER
calpop uses the
.B cairo
renderer unless this variable is set: less memory (about 27 MB
instead of 36 MB with Vulkan).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/calpop/config.toml
Settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/calpop/style.css
Optional extra CSS.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an unknown argument, a configuration error, or when
the desktop does not support layer\-shell.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR waybar (5),
.BR waybar\-clock (5)
.SH LICENSE
MIT.
